# Shell scripts run through `sh` on macOS and Linux, and a carriage return at
# the end of each line breaks them: `set -eu` arrives as `set -eu\r` and the
# shell rejects it. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf converts line endings
# unless told otherwise, and install.sh was uploaded to five releases that way,
# which broke the one-line install on both platforms. Pin them to LF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is happy with either, but it is only ever run on Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
